= Constitution Day

Each year the Senate marks the anniversary of the **Ruusan Reformation**, which ended the last war with the Sith a thousand years ago, disbanded the Republic's armies and placed the Jedi under the Senate's laws. This year the Caucus has the honour of giving the commemorative address.

- @commission: Call for a New Ruusan: a commission to renew the constitution.
- @celebrate: Celebrate a thousand years of peace.
- @corruption: Use the day to attack the Senate's corruption.

@commission
subtitle: Builds support for future constitutional reform.
on-arrival: new_ruusan += 1; senate_resolve += 0.5; faith += 0.5; mod_relation += 2

The address calls on the Senate to renew the Ruusan settlement before a crisis forces its hand. Several blocs agree to join a constitutional commission.

@celebrate
subtitle: Faith in the Republic rises.
on-arrival: faith += 2; fear -= 1

Fireworks light up Coruscant's skylanes. For one evening, the Republic feels young again.

@corruption
subtitle: Less corruption; some blocs are offended.
on-arrival: corruption -= 1.5; guild_relation -= 3; mod_relation -= 2; rc_momentum += 0.5

"The Sith did not defeat the Republic a thousand years ago," the address ends. "Only we can do that."
